<title>UK: De La Rue to buy Philips Smart Cards.</title>
<headline>De La Rue to buy Philips Smart Cards.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>British printing and security products group De La Rue Plc said on Thursday that it has signed a letter of intent to buy Philips Smart Cards &amp; Systems (PSCS).  </p>
<p>It said in a statement that De La Rue Technology and PSCS, which is located in France, have been working together in the UK since June 1993. A joint venture between the two combines De la Rue's magnetic stripe card production and personalisation with PSCS's smart card technology.</p>
<p>De La Rue made the announcement in tandem with Philips Electronics NV, which owns PSCS. The companies did not reveal financial details.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
